IDEAS

This folder keeps the ideas we find in other window managers and
compositors: what they do well that tam-pane should learn from, and what
they do badly that tam-pane should avoid.


ONE FILE PER WINDOW MANAGER

  <name>.md, for example hyprland.md or mangowm.md. Each file has:

    What it is           language, license, base library, scope
    Ideas worth taking   each with a verdict and a reason
    Things to avoid      each with a reason
    Where to look        files or docs to read when we act on an idea

  Verdicts:

    adopt     we want this; it has (or will get) a place in a plan
    consider  promising; needs a closer look or Fred's view
    reject    we decided against it, and the reason says why

  An idea that tam-pane builds gets the plan or version that delivered it,
  for example "adopt (P1, 0.0.4)". When code is taken, not just the idea,
  it is also recorded in UPSTREAM.md.


REFERENCE CLONES

  sources lists the projects we keep a local clone of, so we can read
  their code and follow their fixes. tools/pull-references brings every
  listed clone up to date and clones any that are missing:

    tools/pull-references          pull every listed clone
    tools/pull-references --list   show what is listed and where

  The clones live outside this repository (under ~/Code). Nothing is ever
  pushed or posted to those projects.


HOW DEEP THESE NOTES GO

  The first notes for hyprland.md and mangowm.md come from reading their
  source. The others are starter notes from the projects' known designs,
  to be checked against source before we act on them. A full "survey the
  field" happens only when Fred asks for one.
